{
 "voiceover": "[conversational] Incognito mode doesn't make you private, and most people believe it does.\n\nAll it really does is not save your history and cookies on that device. So the only person you're hiding from is whoever uses your laptop next.\n\n[serious] Your IP address? Still visible. Your internet provider? Still sees where you go. School or office Wi-Fi admins? They can still see it too. And any site you log into knows exactly who you are.\n\n[playful] It's like wearing a mask into a shop. The shopkeeper still sees you.\n\nSo what actually helps? 1: a VPN you trust. It just moves who can see your traffic, so pick carefully. 2: privacy-focused browser settings, like blocking third-party cookies and trackers. 3: separate browser profiles for work, personal and everything else, so your logins never mix.\n\nWhich fix are you trying first: VPN, settings or profiles?\n\nSend this to the friend who thinks Incognito makes them invisible.",
 "title": "INCOGNITO ISN'T PRIVATE",
 "ig_caption": "Incognito mode doesn't make you private. Most people think it does.\n✅ Use a VPN you trust\n✅ Tighten your browser's privacy settings\n✅ Keep separate browser profiles for work and personal\nWhich fix are you trying first? 👇\nSave this for later 📌\nFollow @ihackgrowth for daily AI & tech hacks",
